<h2 id=3D"MedicalCoverage-Web-EntryPoint">Entry Point</h2>
<p>The page found at <code>{ahUrl}/benefits/medical-plan-summary</code></p>
<h2 id=3D"MedicalCoverage-Web-FeatureFlags">Feature Flags</h2>
<p>We have three features that can be shown on this =E2=80=9CBenefits=E2=80=
=9D / =E2=80=9CMedical Coverage=E2=80=9D page. The three features are <stro=
ng>MedPlanSumm</strong>, <strong>PlanDocs</strong>, and <strong>MedicareVid=
eo</strong> (sundaySkyVideo).</p>
<p><u>Logic:</u></p>
<p>If any of those three feature flags are on, we render the page and the e=
nabled feature(s) according to the new design.</p>
<p>If two feature flags are on, the main content area renders either Benefi=
ts List or Plan Docs.</p>
<p>If only one feature flag is on, there is no sidebar and the feature take=
s up the full width.</p>
<p>Miro link: <a class=3D"external-link" data-card-appearance=3D"inline" hr=
ef=3D"https://miro.com/app/board/o9J_ktsswz0=3D/" rel=3D"nofollow">https://=
miro.com/app/board/o9J_ktsswz0=3D/</a></p>
<p><em>This page is to outline the web implementation for this feature for =
all. It breaks down the =E2=80=9CBenefits=E2=80=9D components, their servic=
es, their logic, and details that may be helpful in understanding how it al=
l came together.</em></p>
<h2 id=3D"MedicalCoverage-Web-Components:">Components:</h2>
<h3 id=3D"MedicalCoverage-Web-BenefitsHeader">Benefits Header</h3>
<p>The redesigned header displays different content based on the feature fl=
ags that are turned on but a commercial header with all the flags turned on=
 looks like the screenshot here:</p>
<p>Family:</p><span class=3D"confluence-embedded-file-wrapper image-center-=
wrapper confluence-embedded-manual-size"><img class=3D"confluence-embedded-=
image image-center" width=3D"468" loading=3D"lazy" src=3D"645b20e1893bfaab2=
a31c1f7638488cee221b655d58a55a36e970acd5b6fc99b" data-image-src=3D"https://=
cvsdigital.atlassian.net/wiki/download/attachments/2150170734/Screen%20Shot=
