=3D"lazy" src=3D"ed7fd2a4d877f5aff77401b37cd289854dc90f5ade545ecb6f226db368=
049e9d" data-image-src=3D"https://cvsdigital.atlassian.net/wiki/download/at=
tachments/2150170734/Screen%20Shot%202021-11-11%20at%2011.22.37%20AM.png?ve=
rsion=3D1&amp;modificationDate=3D1636651363877&amp;cacheVersion=3D1&amp;api=
=3Dv2" data-height=3D"172" data-width=3D"864" data-unresolved-comment-count=
=3D"0" data-linked-resource-id=3D"2175666091" data-linked-resource-version=
=3D"1" data-linked-resource-type=3D"attachment" data-linked-resource-defaul=
t-alias=3D"Screen Shot 2021-11-11 at 11.22.37 AM.png" data-base-url=3D"http=
s://cvsdigital.atlassian.net/wiki" data-linked-resource-content-type=3D"ima=
ge/png" data-linked-resource-container-id=3D"2150170734" data-linked-resour=
ce-container-version=3D"31" data-media-id=3D"f78502fe-9874-4825-9490-283862=
084fe6" data-media-type=3D"file" width=3D"468" height=3D"93"></span>
<p>We use the <code>DisplayHeadline</code> component for the page heading (=
h1).</p>
<p>The first names of members are displayed as they exist in the selected a=
ctive policy.</p>
<h4 id=3D"MedicalCoverage-Web-Variations">Variations</h4>
<p>If the member does not have the <code>MedPlanSumm</code> flag on or the =
<code>rollupbenefitlist</code> api returns an error, the membership dates (=
"From {startdate} to {endDate}") come from the <code>appStartup</code> api =
response. As of 11/15/21, this includes pending membership dates.</p>
<p>The header description changes based on the flags. <span class=3D"inline=
-comment-marker" data-ref=3D"78ac292d-3fdd-45ed-9e3b-8cbe584bd893">If </spa=
n><code><span class=3D"inline-comment-marker" data-ref=3D"78ac292d-3fdd-45e=
d-9e3b-8cbe584bd893">MedPlanDocs</span></code><span class=3D"inline-comment=
-marker" data-ref=3D"78ac292d-3fdd-45ed-9e3b-8cbe584bd893"> flag is on</spa=
n>, the content mentions them.</p>
<h5 id=3D"MedicalCoverage-Web-PlanDocsMsgAvail">PlanDocsMsgAvail</h5>
<p>If the user is self-insured (<code>PlanDocsMsgAvail</code> flag) and hav=
e <code>MedPlanDocs</code> on, the header description does not mention plan=
 docs and the Plan Docs tile informs the user that their employer can provi=
de them with the documents.</p>
<div class=3D"confluence-information-macro confluence-information-macro-not=
e">
<span class=3D"aui-icon aui-icon-small aui-iconfont-warning confluence-info=
rmation-macro-icon"></span>
<div class=3D"confluence-information-macro-body">
<p><code>PlanDocsMsgAvail</code> flag can be returned more than once if the=
 memberships have different statuses. i.e:</p>
<p>PlanDocsMsgAvail: { status: "ENABLED", membershipResourceIds: ["A+2"] }<=
br>
PlanDocsMsgAvail: { status: "N/A", membershipResourceIds: ["B+2"] }<br>
PlanDocsMsgAvail: { status: "OFFLINE", membershipResourceIds: ["D+2"] }</p>
<p></p>
<p>So, on the Coverage page, we check if any of them are ENABLED. If they a=
re, we check if the current membershipResourceId (for the selected policy) =
is listed in the membershipResourceIds array. If it is, the selfInsured con=
tent will be rendered. <br><br>
The downside to this feature flag being returned like this from the feature=
s API is that it doesn=E2=80=99t appear to be supported on the features pag=
e so we can=E2=80=99t toggle the flag to test both scenarios =E2=80=93 we n=
ow have to login with users that reflect each scenario as desired.</p>
</div>
</div>
<p>This can be seen with the qa3 user: QA3-S-SEBAGOALLCLAIMS</p>
